    "citation_url": "https://www.revenue.state.mn.us/reciprocity-employee-withholding",
    "notes": "Minnesota and North Dakota have an income tax reciprocity agreement: wages are taxed only by the state of residence. A North Dakota resident working in Minnesota gives the employer Form MWR; a Minnesota resident working in North Dakota gives Form NDW-R (tax.nd.gov).",
    "as_of": "2026-09-28"
  },
  {
    "state_a": "MT",
    "state_b": "ND",
    "direction": "mutual",
    "citation_url": "https://revenue.mt.gov/taxes/withholding-tax/north-dakota-reciprocity",
    "notes": "Montana and North Dakota have an income tax reciprocity agreement for wages, salaries, commissions and employee fees: \"Montana residents earning income in North Dakota pay Montana income tax instead of North Dakota income tax\" (MT DOR). A North Dakota resident working in Montana claims exemption on Form MW-4; a Montana resident working in North Dakota gives Form NDW-R.",
    "as_of": "2026-09-28"
